## Prerequisites

- Terraform and Azure CLI installed
- Contributor permission at Azure subscription scope
- Databricks account admin access
- Your Databricks account ID
{{#unless enable_private_link}}
- `{{azure_admin_user}}` must already be a Databricks account user
{{#unless create_new_vpc}}
- The existing VNet must have room for the generated public and private subnet CIDRs; Terraform creates those subnets, their NSG, and a NAT gateway
{{/unless}}
{{/unless}}

## Authenticate

Authenticate to Azure, select the subscription, and provide the Databricks account ID without storing credentials in `terraform.tfvars`:

```bash
az login
az account set --subscription "{{azure_subscription_id}}"
export TF_VAR_databricks_account_id="<your-databricks-account-id>"
```

For CI/CD, the fetched Terraform also auto-detects service-principal credentials from `ARM_CLIENT_ID`, `ARM_CLIENT_SECRET`, and `ARM_TENANT_ID`. Do not commit credentials.

{{#if enable_private_link}}
## Private Link Topology

This is the upstream Azure Private Link (classic) topology. It creates a dedicated VNet, {{#if enable_nat_gateway}}a NAT gateway, {{/if}}backend and DBFS private endpoints, private DNS zones, storage service endpoints with an endpoint policy, and an account-level NCC for serverless DBFS access. The workspace UI remains available over the public network; front-end Private Link is not configured. Metastore assignment is deliberately disabled.

{{#unless enable_nat_gateway}}
The deployment does not create a NAT gateway, so classic cluster nodes have no general internet egress by default. Ensure all required traffic is covered by the built-in Microsoft.Storage and Microsoft.EventHub service endpoints or routed through your own firewall/network virtual appliance (NVA). If clusters need customer-managed storage through the storage service endpoint, add its full Azure resource ID to `service_endpoint_policy_storage_accounts` before applying.
{{/unless}}
{{else}}
## Unity Catalog

The canonical upstream VNet-injection source creates or attaches a metastore and provisions the selected UC storage account, storage credential, external location, and catalog. The storage account enforces TLS 1.2, infrastructure encryption, and disabled public blob access. Optional cluster creation is disabled.
{{/if}}

## Deploy

All Terraform files are at the ZIP root:

```bash
terraform init
terraform validate
terraform plan -var-file=terraform.tfvars
terraform apply -var-file=terraform.tfvars
```

Review the plan carefully before applying it.

## Cleanup

```bash
terraform destroy -var-file=terraform.tfvars
```

Destroying infrastructure can permanently remove workspace resources and data.

